  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">#Promoting and strengthening the quality infrastructure system for the sustainability and competitiveness of Paraguay in the agro-industrial sector (SiCalidad Paraguay)#.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EU is developing a programme called #Support for the promotion and strengthening of the sustainability and competitiveness of Paraguay&#xb4;s agricultural, forestry and agro-industrial value chains# to contribute consolidating Paraguay&#xb4;s insertion in the international trade dynamics by promoting and strengthening sustainability and competitiveness through enhancing quality infrastructure and traceability of prioritized value chains as a mean for the diversification and innovation of key sectors for the economy.  It is envisaged that UNIDO implements areas related to Quality Infrastructure as a mean to improve sustainability and actions to inc rease quality culture and sustainability awareness, and support Business Intermediary Organizations (BIOs) to provide competitive services to the selected value chains related to quality, certifications, technology development, innovation and sustainable practices. The project will build on the experiences and achievements of the previous EU funded project named #Support for the Improvement of the Competitiveness of MSMEs and the Business Environment in Paraguay# known as MiPYME COMPITE in the areas implemented by UNIDO TCS/SME/CQC.  MiPYME COMPITE encompassed over 400 MSMEs across rural and industrial sectors, underscoring the pivotal role of quality standards in shaping c</narrative>
  </description>
